The issue is that the current implementation pads every column with spaces, even for positions beyond the longest line's actual content. The tests expect no trailing spaces on each output row.

I'll track the last row index that contributes a real character to each output row, then trim trailing spaces.

Transpose.java
```java
public class Transpose {
    public String transpose(String toTranspose) {
        String[] lines = toTranspose.split("\n", -1);
        int maxLen = 0;
        for (String line : lines) {
            maxLen = Math.max(maxLen, line.length());
        }

        StringBuilder[] result = new StringBuilder[maxLen];
        for (int i = 0; i < maxLen; i++) {
            result[i] = new StringBuilder();
        }
        int[] lastReal = new int[maxLen];
        for (int i = 0; i < maxLen; i++) {
            lastReal[i] = -1;
        }

        for (int col = 0; col < maxLen; col++) {
            for (int row = 0; row < lines.length; row++) {
                if (col < lines[row].length()) {
                    result[col].append(lines[row].charAt(col));
                    lastReal[col] = Math.max(lastReal[col], row);
                }
            }
        }

        StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder();
        for (int i = 0; i < maxLen; i++) {
            int last = lastReal[i];
            if (last >= 0) {
                sb.append(result[i].substring(0, last + 1));
            }
            if (i < maxLen - 1) {
                sb.append('\n');
            }
        }

        return sb.toString();
    }
}
```
