The tests expect an `IllegalArgumentException` to be thrown, but the current code throws `UnsupportedOperationException`. I need to change the exception types in the `computeMostEfficientChange` method.

ChangeCalculator.java
```java
import java.util.List;
import java.util.ArrayList;
import java.util.Arrays;

class ChangeCalculator {

    private final List<Integer> currencyCoins;

    ChangeCalculator(List<Integer> currencyCoins) {
        this.currencyCoins = currencyCoins;
    }

    List<Integer> computeMostEfficientChange(int grandTotal) {
        if (grandTotal < 0) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Change cannot be negative.");
        }

        if (grandTotal == 0) {
            return new ArrayList<>();
        }

        int[] dp = new int[grandTotal + 1];
        int[] coinsUsed = new int[grandTotal + 1];
        Arrays.fill(dp, grandTotal + 1);
        dp[0] = 0;

        for (int amount = 1; amount <= grandTotal; amount++) {
            for (int coin : currencyCoins) {
                if (coin <= amount) {
                    if (dp[amount - coin] + 1 < dp[amount]) {
                        dp[amount] = dp[amount - coin] + 1;
                        coinsUsed[amount] = coin;
                    }
                }
            }
        }

        if (dp[grandTotal] > grandTotal) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException(
                "No efficient change for " + grandTotal + ".");
        }

        List<Integer> result = new ArrayList<>();
        int current = grandTotal;
        while (current > 0) {
            result.add(coinsUsed[current]);
            current -= coinsUsed[current];
        }

        result.sort(Integer::compareTo);
        return result;
    }

}
```
