The error `invalid rank: 4�` indicates that the card parsing is failing because 
the card strings contain multi-byte UTF-8 suit characters (like ♤, ♡, ♢, ♧). 
When using `c[len(c)-1]` on a string with multi-byte runes, it only takes the 
last byte, not the last rune.



I'll fix the parsing to use `utf8.RuneInStr` to properly handle the suit 
characters.



