Ok, I understand the request. I'll refactor the tree building algorithm in `BuildTree.java`.

The current implementation is slow (O(n²) or worse) and ugly. I'll rewrite it to be cleaner and more efficient:

1. Validate records first (checking for invalid parent IDs, self-referential non-root nodes, etc.)
2. Build the tree in a single pass where possible
3. Handle edge cases properly

Here's my refactored version:

BuildTree.java
```java
import java.util.ArrayList;
import java.util.HashMap;
import java.util.Map;

class BuildTree {

    TreeNode buildTree(ArrayList<Record> records) throws InvalidRecordsException {
        if (records.isEmpty()) {
            return null;
        }

        // Validate record count and IDs
        if (records.size() != getUniqueRecordIds(records).size()) {
            throw new InvalidRecordsException("Invalid Records");
        }

        // Build node map
        Map<Integer, TreeNode> nodeMap = new HashMap<>();
        for (Record record : records) {
            nodeMap.put(record.getRecordId(), new TreeNode(record.getRecordId()));
        }

        // Establish parent-child relationships
        for (Record record : records) {
            int parentId = record.getParentId();
            int recordId = record.getRecordId();

            if (recordId == 0) {
                // Root node - no parent
                if (parentId != 0) {
                    throw new InvalidRecordsException("Invalid Records");
                }
                continue;
            }

            if (parentId >= recordId) {
                throw new InvalidRecordsException("Invalid Records");
            }

            TreeNode parent = nodeMap.get(parentId);
            TreeNode child = nodeMap.get(recordId);

            if (parent == null || child == null) {
                throw new InvalidRecordsException("Invalid Records");
            }

            parent.getChildren().add(child);
        }

        // Return root node
        return nodeMap.get(0);
    }

    private ArrayList<Integer> getUniqueRecordIds(ArrayList<Record> records) {
        ArrayList<Integer> ids = new ArrayList<>();
        for (Record record : records) {
            if (!ids.contains(record.getRecordId())) {
                ids.add(record.getRecordId());
            }
        }
        return ids;
    }
}
```
