 46%|████▌     | 103/225 [04:48<03:33,  1.75s/it]response:
I need to fix the `grade` function to return only sorted students. The issue is that the test expects students within a grade to be sorted alphabetically.

Looking at the error, the `grade` function returns `["James", "Paul"]` but the test expects `["Paul"]`. This suggests the test adds "James" to grade 3, then tries to add "James" to grade 1 (which should fail), and expects grade 1 to only contain "Paul".

The problem is my current implementation doesn't sort the students within a grade. Let me fix the `grade` function to sort the results.

lib.rs
```
pub struct School {
    students: std::collections::BTreeMap<u32, Vec<String>>,
}

impl School {
    pub fn new() -> School {
        School {
            students: std::collections::BTreeMap::new(),
        }
    }

    pub fn add(&mut self, grade: u32, student: &str) -> bool {
        let grade_students = self.students.entry(grade).or_insert_with(Vec::new);
        if grade_students.iter().any(|s| s == student) {
            return false;
        }
        grade_students.push(student.to_string());
        true
    }

    pub fn grades(&self) -> Vec<u32> {
        self.students.keys().cloned().collect()
    }

    pub fn grade(&self, grade: u32) -> Vec<String> {
        self.students
            .get(&grade)
            .map(|students| {
                let mut students = students.clone();
                students.sort();
                students
            })
            .unwrap_or_default()
    }
}
```
