I'll analyze the test failures and refactor the code to be cleaner and more efficient.

The current implementation has issues:
1. It uses a slow O(n²) duplicate check via `getUniqueRecordIds`
2. It doesn't validate that IDs are continuous (0 to n-1)
3. It doesn't detect duplicate records properly

Here's the refactored version:

BuildTree.java
```java
import java.util.ArrayList;
import java.util.HashSet;
import java.util.Set;

class BuildTree {

    TreeNode buildTree(ArrayList<Record> records) throws InvalidRecordsException {
        if (records.isEmpty()) {
            return null;
        }

        int expectedSize = records.size();
        Set<Integer> uniqueIds = new HashSet<>();
        for (Record record : records) {
            int id = record.getRecordId();
            if (id < 0 || id >= expectedSize) {
                throw new InvalidRecordsException("Invalid Records");
            }
            if (!uniqueIds.add(id)) {
                throw new InvalidRecordsException("Invalid Records");
            }
        }

        if (uniqueIds.size() != expectedSize) {
            throw new InvalidRecordsException("Invalid Records");
        }

        // Build node map
        TreeNode[] nodes = new TreeNode[expectedSize];
        for (int i = 0; i < expectedSize; i++) {
            nodes[i] = new TreeNode(i);
        }

        // Establish parent-child relationships
        for (Record record : records) {
            int parentId = record.getParentId();
            int recordId = record.getRecordId();

            if (recordId == 0) {
                // Root node - no parent
                if (parentId != 0) {
                    throw new InvalidRecordsException("Invalid Records");
                }
                continue;
            }

            if (parentId >= recordId) {
                throw new InvalidRecordsException("Invalid Records");
            }

            nodes[recordId].getParent().getChildren().add(nodes[parentId]);
        }

        // Return root node
        return nodes[0];
    }
}
```
