Actually, let me reconsider. The standard pattern for nested next_permutation 
loops is:

```
do {
    do {
        ...
    } while (next_permutation(...));
} while (next_permutation(...));
```

When the inner loop's next_permutation returns false, the array is reset to 
sorted {0,1,2,3,4}. So after the inner loop, the array IS sorted. Then the outer
loop's next_permutation works correctly.

