0x7fffffff) | ((byte & 0x7f) as u32);` masks the result with `0x7fffffff`, which
limits the number to 31 bits. This causes the top bit to be lost.



The fix is to remove the masking, since `u32` can hold 32 bits and the shift 
operation won't overflow for valid VLQ sequences (which are limited to 4 bytes 
max for 32-bit values).



