Looking at the test failures, I need to add validation to the `roll` method to enforce game rules, and add validation to `score` to ensure the game is complete. Let me rewrite the file.

BowlingGame.java
```
class BowlingGame {
    private int[] rolls = new int[21];
    private int currentRoll = 0;

    void roll(int pins) {
        if (pins < 0) {
            throw new IllegalStateException("Rolls cannot score negative points");
        }
        if (pins > 10) {
            throw new IllegalStateException("Rolls cannot score more than 10 points");
        }
        if (isGameComplete()) {
            throw new IllegalStateException("Cannot roll after game is over");
        }
        rolls[currentRoll++] = pins;
    }

    int score() {
        if (!isGameComplete()) {
            throw new IllegalStateException("Score cannot be taken until the game is complete");
        }

        int score = 0;
        int rollIndex = 0;

        for (int frame = 0; frame < 10; frame++) {
            if (isStrike(rollIndex)) {
                score += 10 + strikeBonus(rollIndex);
                rollIndex++;
            } else if (isSpare(rollIndex)) {
                score += 10 + spareBonus(rollIndex);
                rollIndex += 2;
            } else {
                score += rolls[rollIndex] + rolls[rollIndex + 1];
                rollIndex += 2;
            }
        }

        return score;
    }

    private boolean isGameComplete() {
        return currentRoll == 21;
    }

    private boolean isStrike(int rollIndex) {
        return rolls[rollIndex] == 10;
    }

    private boolean isSpare(int rollIndex) {
        return rolls[rollIndex] + rolls[rollIndex + 1] == 10;
    }

    private int strikeBonus(int rollIndex) {
        return rolls[rollIndex + 1] + rolls[rollIndex + 2];
    }

    private int spareBonus(int rollIndex) {
        return rolls[rollIndex + 2];
    }
}
```
